-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Sabre Wulf
  Publisher   Ultimate, 1984
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Sabre Wulf (1984)(Ultimate Play The Game).z80
  MD5         d8fb649ba5d8fa086cac43d0cd1c497e

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The Spec256 conversion's colours on every figure: khaki
              Sabreman, coloured parrot, pale spider, dusky scorpion, grey
              rhino; the jungle unchanged. No white outlines or edges. Painted
              colours are fixed, so Sabreman no longer changes colour with the
              orchids. Source: Enhanced colours: from the Spec256 conversion
              (the Spectrum Magic package, credited to Spec256), painter not
              established.

  Pace        original (+1.67% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless; probe 39453
              (the end of a round of the object loop: enemy pace); input keyed
              to rounds; 10 trials per scene; a fixture with the game's time
              sources read from its round counter in both runs)

  Changes     1.0: figures as Next sprites; Sinclair's 48K ROM as the whole
              alt ROM, so the game starts from its own BASIC; the game's speed
              restored after every hook; R kept as the original's; faster
              hooks with a frame cache; the Spec256 conversion's colours as
              the Enhanced set. 1.1: QAOP + Space option

  Note        Keys: any key on the loading screen, then 0 on the menu (1 or 2
              players, 3-6 controls). In play Q left, W right, E up, R down, T
              fight, SPACE pause. With QAOP + Space on (menu, off by default;
              keyboard chosen, 3): Q up, A down, O left, P right, Space fight,
              Caps Shift pause (Space or Caps Shift resumes); W, E, R and T do
              nothing; joysticks move and fight as before, and pause on Caps
              Shift too. Every moving figure is a Next sprite in the game's
              own colours, the look the owner approved; the jungle, panel and
              text keep the original's colours. The hooks cost about 1.7
              percent of the game's pace (enemies a little slower than the
              original, never faster); the game has no frame cap, so this
              could not be repaid. It starts from the tape's own BASIC, as on
              a 48K. Cheats from the archive's POKEs for this release;
              dropped: Infinite Lives (an RST 38 at each death, and the two
              below do it cleanly), Keep SabreMan cyan (sets colour 186 and
              stops every orchid effect ending), Immunity (lives still lost),
              Less Animals, No destructible Enemies and Floating rhinos (no
              effect seen in the simulator), See Ending and Paralyzed Enemies
              (the game freezes), Lives and Invincibility to jungle animals
              (ask for a value). Not tested on hardware.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  [P1]Infinite lives
   2  [P2]Infinite lives
   3  Less enemies
   4  Always walk fast
   5  "Ghost" jungle

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

